# Stand-alone — base configuration (ADR-090 D-2).
# Layer order, lowest first:  base.env  <  profile.<name>.env  <  .env.secrets
#   < real environment. ADR-008's inject_env(overwrite=False) means an
# already-set variable always wins, so nothing here can clobber an operator.
#
# No secrets in this file. `standalone.sh bootstrap` generates .env.secrets.

COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=ai4s-standalone

# ── storage ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
POSTGRES_DB=umrs
S3_BUCKET=r4-data

# ── model backend (a): ollama, local and offline at runtime ───────────────
# Maintainer decision 2026-10-08: ollama with small free models. Small models
# are preferred on a small machine; everything here is meant to be changed.
#
# Pull a model before first use (this needs network; the runtime network does
# not have any):   ./standalone.sh model pull llama3.2:3b
# List what is staged:                           ./standalone.sh model list
OLLAMA_IMAGE=docker.io/ollama/ollama:latest
# The chat model the agent harness uses. It MUST support tool calling, or the
# R4 companion cannot call tools. Known-good small options:
#   llama3.2:3b     ~2.0 GB   tools  — good default on a laptop
#   qwen2.5:7b      ~4.7 GB   tools  — stronger, needs ~8 GB RAM
#   qwen2.5:14b     ~9.0 GB   tools  — for a workstation with VRAM to spare
STANDALONE_CHAT_MODEL=llama3.2:3b
STANDALONE_CHAT_MEM=8g
# Keep the model resident between agent turns; a cold reload per request makes
# a multi-step loop unusable.
OLLAMA_KEEP_ALIVE=30m
# The window ollama actually serves. Its own default is 4096 regardless of the
# model, but the companion's tool set alone is ~10.5k prompt tokens — at 4096
# the tool list is silently truncated. Keep this equal to the max_model_len the
# endpoint registry row advertises.
OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH=32768
# Concurrent requests. KV cache scales with context x parallel: llama3.2:3b at
# 32k needs ~6.0 GiB with 1 slot and ~9.6 GiB with 2. Raise it only together
# with STANDALONE_CHAT_MEM, or on a GPU host with VRAM to spare.
# Recommended on a capable host (ADR-093 MD-11, decided 2026-10-11): >= 16 GB
# RAM or a GPU -> OLLAMA_NUM_PARALLEL=2, so a side call (router, extraction,
# sufficiency) gets its own slot instead of evicting the agent's. The default
# stays 1. This file reaches only the CONTAINER ollama; set it in env/local.env
# with STANDALONE_CHAT_MEM=12g. A native ollama (STANDALONE_MODEL_HOST=native,
# reached at host.containers.internal:11434) is not managed by compose: set it
# on the host (macOS app: launchctl setenv OLLAMA_NUM_PARALLEL 2, then reopen
# Ollama; CLI: OLLAMA_NUM_PARALLEL=2 ollama serve). `doctor` shows the value.
OLLAMA_NUM_PARALLEL=1

# ── embeddings (ADR-090 D-4: decoupled from the chat backend) ──────────────
# The umrs image bundles intfloat/e5-base-v2 (768-d) at
# /opt/umrs/models/e5-base-v2 and uses it while this is unset (maintainer
# decision 2026-10-09), for knowledge ingest and the RAG query encoder alike.
# Another sentence-transformers model: stage it, then point at it in
# env/local.env —
#   ./standalone.sh embedder pull intfloat/multilingual-e5-base me5b
#   UMRS_KNOWLEDGE_EMBED_MODEL=/models/me5b
# UMRS_KNOWLEDGE_EMBED_MODEL=

# ── retrieval (ADR-093; 2026-10-10) ────────────────────────────────────────
# compose.yaml maps every knob below with the default shown, so nothing here
# needs setting. To change one, put it in env/local.env and run
# `./standalone.sh up` (`up --dev` for dev): --env-file only interpolates when
# a container is created, so `restart` does NOT pick up an env change.
# Constants are tuned on the SciFact tune split only (benchmarks/retrieval).
#   UMRS_RAG_FINAL_K_MAX=4        passages kept after the cut
#   UMRS_RAG_POOL=50              candidates before fusion and the cut
#   UMRS_RAG_PER_ARTIFACT=2       passages per source document
#   UMRS_RAG_LEXICAL=auto         auto|on|off (needs migration 0120 + backfill)
#   UMRS_RAG_MERGE=off            neighbour merge after the cut (S2 gate)
#   UMRS_RAG_TAIL_CHARS=200       the merge's tail floor (characters)
#   UMRS_RAG_DELTA=0.03  UMRS_RAG_GAMMA=0.015         the dense cut
#   UMRS_RAG_Z_SUFFICIENT=3.0  UMRS_RAG_Z_PARTIAL=2.0  UMRS_RAG_NULL_P=0.05
#   UMRS_RAG_LEX_RATIO=0.5  UMRS_RAG_LEX_COVERAGE=0.5   the fused cut and the
#   UMRS_RAG_LEX_HIT_IDF=3.0  UMRS_RAG_LEX_MIN_TERMS=2  lexical sufficiency rule
#   UMRS_RAG_FUSION=rrf           rrf|convex (C6's measured alternative)
#   UMRS_RAG_W_DENSE=1.0  UMRS_RAG_W_LEX=1.0  UMRS_RAG_W_IDENT=0.5  (RRF)
#   UMRS_RAG_ANSWER_MAX_TOKENS=400  UMRS_RAG_PACK_ORDER=rank
#   UMRS_RAG_PACK_INSTRUCTION=soft
#   UMRS_RAG_PROFILE=auto         auto|small|medium|large (D-14): the reading
#       model's profile sizes k_max, pool, merge, the partial cap and the
#       answer limit; auto = the registry model's size (llama3.2:3b: small,
#       the values above; rikyu's kimi-k3 and glm-5.3: large). A request's
#       `profile` (R4 sends its session model's) wins.
#   UMRS_RAG_GRAPH_LANE=auto      off|auto|on: graph bridges (D-14); auto = on
#       only when the extraction model is large AND the lane is measured
#       (below), so off on this 3B stack; any other value is off
#   UMRS_RAG_GRAPH_LANE_MEASURED=0  1 once the lane passes its multi-hop
#       probe (maintainer); until then auto stays off even at a large site
#   UMRS_KNOWLEDGE_CHUNK_SCHEME=fixed-v0   (sent-v1 waits for the S7 gate)
# EVAL ONLY, rag container: how a query reaches e5. `fixed` = `query: <q>`;
# `b0` = baseline B0's `passage: query: <q>` (the double prefix fixed
# 2026-10-10), for measuring the fix alone and checking legacy parity with
# B0. /rag/stats reports `query_prefix` and `query_encoding`.
#   UMRS_RAG_QUERY_PREFIX=fixed
# The offline cross-encoder (rag container). Off while empty; stage it once
# (needs network), then name the staged DIRECTORY — a hub id is refused:
#   ./standalone.sh reranker pull          # -> /models/ms-marco-MiniLM-L6-v2
#   UMRS_RAG_RERANKER_MODEL=/models/ms-marco-MiniLM-L6-v2
#   UMRS_RAG_RERANKER_THREADS=2
# `rerank=auto` uses it only when UMRS_RAG_RERANK_DEFAULT=on (set only if the
# S4 gate passes); `rerank=on` per request uses it whenever it is staged.
#   UMRS_RAG_RERANK_DEFAULT=off   UMRS_RAG_RERANK_MODE=replace  (|interpolate)
#   UMRS_RAG_RERANKER_TIMEOUT=10  seconds per /rag/rerank call
# The reranker-mode cut (S4): keep while p >= P_MIN and logit >= logit_1 -
# WINDOW, then cut at the largest gap >= GAP; sufficient when p_1 >=
# P_SUFFICIENT.
#   UMRS_RAG_RERANK_P_MIN=0.10  UMRS_RAG_RERANK_WINDOW=4.0
#   UMRS_RAG_RERANK_GAP=2.0     UMRS_RAG_RERANK_P_SUFFICIENT=0.5
# The image never bakes a reranker in (ADR-093 MD-3, decided 2026-10-11):
# `reranker pull` is the only way MiniLM reaches this stack.
# Schema for the lexical lane (migration 0120):  ./standalone.sh migrate
# then fill (and, with --verify, re-check) the column without a re-embed:
#   ./standalone.sh exec umrs python -m umrs.knowledge.retrieval.backfill \
#       --project P [--graph G] [--dry-run] [--verify]
# Orphan chunk/file nodes from before wave F's one-transaction writer (MD-17):
#   ./standalone.sh orphan-repair [--project P]...           # dry run, counts
#   ./standalone.sh orphan-repair --apply [--project P]...   # deletes

# ── MCP (ADR-090 D-5: Hatch/Hatchling, identical to remote) ────────────────
# The in-repo registry is a complete local substitute, verified with networking
# disabled: _local_reference_path (hatchling.py) detects a filesystem path and
# _install_from_registry_tree installs without git. r4 reads it on the HOST, so
# an env file here cannot reach it. Export it in your shell (README "MCP"):
#   HATCH_REGISTRY_URL=<repo>/mcp-servers/hatch-registry
# MCP on this stack: the Hatch runtime runs on the host, UMRS in a container.
# Export these in the shell where you run `r4 mcp hatch connect` (see README):
#   R4_HATCH_BIND_HOST=0.0.0.0  R4_HATCH_ADVERTISE_HOST=host.containers.internal
# A non-loopback bind gets a per-runtime token that UMRS presents on each call.
STANDALONE_MCP_DIR=./mcp
